3. LICENSE ACTIVATION, DEVICE BINDING, AND SERVER VERIFICATION
================================================================================
(a) Unique License Keys: Certain tiers and features of the Software require a
    unique License Key for activation. Each License Key is cryptographically
    validated and tied to the application's package identity and device fingerprint.
(b) Device Activation Limits: Each License Key is subject to a maximum device
    activation quota maintained and enforced by Licensor's licensing servers.
(c) Server-Side Validation: The Software periodically verifies license status,
    entitlements, and revocation with Licensor's authoritative license servers
    over secure HTTPS connections.
(d) Offline Grace Period: The Software allows continued operation during temporary
    offline periods for up to seven (7) days from the last successful server
    validation. Following the expiration of the offline grace period, active
    internet connectivity is required to re-validate entitlements. Tampering with
    the system clock or monotonic timers will immediately invalidate the offline
    grace token.
(e) Revocation: Licensor reserves the right to immediately revoke, suspend, or
    terminate any License Key found to be compromised, shared publicly, used on
    excessive devices, or associated with fraudulent activities.

