    guest kernels (such as the Linux Kernel licensed under GNU GPLv2, Ubuntu
    Cloud Images provided by Canonical Ltd., and Alpine Linux).
(b) Preservation of Open-Source Licenses: Nothing in this proprietary Agreement
    is intended to restrict, expand, or override the rights granted to Licensee
    under the respective open-source licenses governing such external guest
    components. All third-party copyrights, licenses, notices, and source code
    availability terms are strictly preserved and accessible in the Software's
    "Licenses & OS" registry.
(c) No Viral Encumbrance: The proprietary emulator logic, user interface, and
    application framework of MobileVM run in Android user-space and communicate
    with guest operating systems solely across virtual hardware boundaries (MMIO,
    UART, and virtual CPU instructions). No proprietary code is incorporated into
    or statically linked with the GPL-licensed guest Linux kernel.

